.TH mm2_chain 1 "18 February 2026" "minimap2-2.24" "Bioinformatics tools"
.SH NAME
.PP
mm2_chain \- chain seed anchors for minimap2 staged pipeline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.B mm2_chain
.RB [ -x
.IR preset ]
.RB [ options ]
.I reference.fa
.B -s
.I seeds.json
.B -o
.I output.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B mm2_chain
is a CLI tool that performs the chaining stage of the minimap2 mapping
pipeline. It connects seed anchors (from
.BR mm2_seed (1))
into co-linear chains using dynamic programming, and outputs them in JSON
format for downstream processing by
.BR mm2_align (1).
.PP
This tool supports GPU acceleration for chaining via the
.B --use-gpu
option, which requires a GPU configuration file.
.PP
For end-to-end alignment workflows, use
.BR minimap2 (1)
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Required arguments
.TP 10
.I reference.fa
Reference FASTA file (used to load the minimizer index).
.TP
.BI -s \ FILE
Input seeds JSON file (produced by
.BR mm2_seed (1)).
.TP
.BI -o \ FILE
Output chains JSON file.
.SS Preset
.TP 10
.BI -x \ STR
Preset configuration. Available presets:
.BR map-ont ,
.BR map-pb ,
.BR map-hifi ,
.BR asm5 / asm10 / asm20 ,
.BR sr ,
.BR splice .
.SS Indexing options
.TP 10
.BI -k \ INT
K-mer size [from input or 15].
.TP
.BI -w \ INT
Minimizer window size [from input or 10].
.SS Chaining options
.TP 10
.BI -g \ INT
Maximum gap in reference/query [5000]. Stop chain extension if there
are no minimizers within this many base pairs.
.TP
.BI -G \ INT
Maximum gap on reference, overrides
.B -g
[0 = use
.BR -g ].
.TP
.BI -b \ INT
Bandwidth for DP chaining [500].
.TP
.BI -B \ INT
Long-join bandwidth for ultra-long reads [0 = disabled].
.TP
.BI -n \ INT
Minimum anchor count per chain [3]. Discard chains with fewer anchors.
.TP
.BI -c \ INT
Minimum chain score [40]. Discard chains with a chaining score below
this threshold.
.TP
.B -r
Use RMQ (Range Minimum Query) algorithm. Faster for ultra-long reads.
Incompatible with GPU chaining.
.SS Advanced chaining options
.TP 10
.BI --max-chain-skip \ INT
Max anchors to skip during chaining [25]. A heuristic that stops
chaining early. Set to a large number to disable.
.TP
.BI --max-chain-iter \ INT
Max chaining DP iterations [5000]. Limits quadratic time complexity
in the worst case.
.TP
.BI --chain-gap-scale \ FLOAT
Gap cost scaling factor [1.0].
.TP
.BI --chain-skip-scale \ FLOAT
Skip cost scaling factor [1.0].
.SS GPU options
.TP 10
.B --use-gpu
Enable GPU acceleration for chaining. Requires a GPU configuration file.
Incompatible with RMQ algorithm
.RB ( -r ).
.TP
.BI --gpu-config \ FILE
GPU configuration JSON file [gpu_config.json]. Specifies batch sizes,
kernel parameters, and memory limits. See
.BR minimap2 (1)
for configuration details.
.SS Other options
.TP 10
.B -h
Show help message.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.PP
Output is a JSON file containing chained anchors for each query:
.PP
.nf
{
  "queries": [{
    "name": "read1",
    "n_chains": 1,
    "chains": [{
      "score": 345,
      "length": 42
    }]
  }]
}
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Basic chaining with ONT preset:
.PP
.RS 4
.B mm2_chain -x map-ont ref.fa -s seeds.json -o chains.json
.RE
.PP
GPU-accelerated chaining:
.PP
.RS 4
.B mm2_chain --use-gpu --gpu-config gpu_config.json ref.fa -s seeds.json -o chains.json
.RE
.PP
Custom chaining parameters:
.PP
.RS 4
.B mm2_chain -x map-ont -g 10000 -b 1000 -n 2 -c 20 ref.fa -s seeds.json -o chains.json
.RE
.PP
Using RMQ for ultra-long reads:
.PP
.RS 4
.B mm2_chain -x map-ont -r ref.fa -s seeds.json -o chains.json
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
mm2_seed(1), mm2_align(1), minimap2(1)
